WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.463
This is your explainer on the family, the family home,

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:08.326
and paternity and filiation: Articles one forty-nine to one eighty-two

00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:11.416
of the Family Code, for Attorney Uribe's class.

00:00:11.946 --> 00:00:13.290
We'll go in four parts.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.945
First, the family and the earnest efforts rule.

00:00:16.125 --> 00:00:17.597
Second, the family home.

00:00:17.777 --> 00:00:20.635
Third, legitimacy and the action to impugn it.

00:00:20.815 --> 00:00:23.610
And fourth, proof of filiation and legitimation.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.198
Along the way, I'll flag Sir's favorite traps, and the points

00:00:27.198 --> 00:00:30.297
where his view differs from the codal or from Tolentino.

00:00:31.377 --> 00:00:33.873
Article one forty-nine sets the policy.

00:00:34.053 --> 00:00:36.420
The family is the foundation of the

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.448
nation and a basic social institution.

00:00:38.628 --> 00:00:42.524
So family relations are governed by law, and no custom,

00:00:42.524 --> 00:00:46.030
practice or agreement destructive of the family is recognized.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.733
The trap is simple.

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:51.124
If a statement says family relations are governed by custom,

00:00:51.124 --> 00:00:54.335
or by the agreement of the parties, it is false.

00:00:54.515 --> 00:00:55.773
It's law that governs.

00:00:56.303 --> 00:00:59.652
Arroyo versus Court of Appeals shows the policy at work.

00:00:59.832 --> 00:01:03.322
In an adultery case, once the offended spouse files the

00:01:03.322 --> 00:01:06.811
complaint, control passes to the public prosecutor, and a pardon

00:01:06.811 --> 00:01:09.603
given after filing does not end the case.

00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:12.609
The State's interest in marriage and the family is,

00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:15.436
in the Court's words, of the most fundamental kind.

00:01:16.517 --> 00:01:20.261
Article one fifty lists who counts as family: husband and

00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:24.006
wife, parents and children, other ascendants and descendants, and brothers

00:01:24.006 --> 00:01:27.376
and sisters, whether of the full or half blood.

00:01:27.905 --> 00:01:28.737
Count them.

00:01:28.917 --> 00:01:29.856
There are four.

00:01:30.036 --> 00:01:34.558
Some student reviewers print only three and drop other ascendants and descendants.

00:01:34.738 --> 00:01:38.301
That item matters: grandparents and grandchildren are family.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:42.918
Everyone else is a stranger for this purpose: in-laws, step

00:01:42.918 --> 00:01:46.596
relations, uncles and aunts, nephews and nieces, and cousins.

00:01:46.776 --> 00:01:49.496
The list is exclusive and is strictly construed,

00:01:49.496 --> 00:01:52.216
as the Court said in Gayon versus Gayon.

00:01:53.297 --> 00:01:56.326
Article one fifty-one is the earnest efforts rule.

00:01:56.506 --> 00:02:00.110
A suit between members of the same family will not

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:03.714
prosper unless the verified complaint or petition shows that earnest

00:02:03.714 --> 00:02:06.597
efforts toward a compromise were made and failed.

00:02:06.777 --> 00:02:10.318
But the rule does not apply to matters that cannot be compromised.

00:02:10.848 --> 00:02:12.149
Run three questions.

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:14.228
First, are all the parties family?

00:02:14.408 --> 00:02:18.056
If even one party is a stranger, like the sister-in-law

00:02:18.056 --> 00:02:21.704
and nephews in Gayon, Article one fifty-one does not apply.

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.602
Second, is the subject compromisable?

00:02:24.782 --> 00:02:29.851
Under Article twenty thirty-five of the Civil Code, you cannot compromise civil

00:02:29.851 --> 00:02:34.920
status, the validity of a marriage or legal separation, any ground for

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.566
legal separation, future support, the jurisdiction of courts, or future legitime.

00:02:39.746 --> 00:02:42.701
So in Wainwright-Versoza, an action for future

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:45.655
support needed no allegation of earnest efforts.

00:02:46.185 --> 00:02:48.489
Third, did the defendant raise it on time?

00:02:48.669 --> 00:02:53.064
Earnest efforts is a condition precedent, not a jurisdictional requirement.

00:02:53.244 --> 00:02:56.594
If it isn't raised in a motion to dismiss or the answer,

00:02:56.594 --> 00:02:59.665
it is waived, and the court cannot dismiss on its own.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:02.085
That's Heirs of Favis versus Gonzales.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.514
Sir tested this with a situationer.

00:03:04.694 --> 00:03:07.758
A, the illegitimate child of X, sued X and

00:03:07.758 --> 00:03:10.823
X's wife Y for support, and X raised lack

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.547
of earnest efforts only in the Supreme Court.

00:03:13.727 --> 00:03:16.837
The defense fails: it's only a ground for a motion

00:03:16.837 --> 00:03:19.636
to dismiss, and Y, the stepmother, is a stranger.

00:03:19.816 --> 00:03:23.059
And remember his warning: don't assume facts that aren't given.

00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:25.760
Part two, the family home.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.628
Under Article one fifty-two, it is constituted jointly by the husband

00:03:29.628 --> 00:03:32.980
and wife, or by an unmarried head of a family.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.276
It is the dwelling house where they reside,

00:03:35.276 --> 00:03:37.128
and the land on which it stands.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:42.179
Article one fifty-six says it must be on property of the absolute

00:03:42.179 --> 00:03:46.699
community or conjugal partnership, or on the exclusive property of either spouse

00:03:46.699 --> 00:03:50.843
with that spouse's consent, or on the unmarried head's own property.

00:03:51.023 --> 00:03:55.418
There's one exception: property bought on a conditional sale on installments.

00:03:55.598 --> 00:03:58.222
And a person may have only one family home.

00:03:58.751 --> 00:04:00.266
Here is a conflict to know.

00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:04.222
In recitation, Sir argues that the house alone should qualify.

00:04:04.402 --> 00:04:06.930
Many families in Metro Manila live in

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.458
condominium units and don't own the land.

00:04:09.988 --> 00:04:13.640
But Sir's own midterm key marked false a statement saying the

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.292
dwelling house or the land, because the codal says house and

00:04:17.292 --> 00:04:20.612
land, and the Supreme Court requires ownership of the land.

00:04:20.792 --> 00:04:22.883
The twenty eleven bar answer agrees.

00:04:23.063 --> 00:04:25.217
So on a written quiz, follow the codal.

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.467
In recitation, give both views.

00:04:28.547 --> 00:04:30.467
When is a family home constituted?

00:04:30.647 --> 00:04:33.220
Article one fifty-three: from the time it

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.426
is occupied as a family residence.

00:04:35.606 --> 00:04:37.697
And it stays a family home as

00:04:37.697 --> 00:04:39.787
long as any beneficiary actually lives there.

00:04:40.317 --> 00:04:41.320
That's a change.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.903
Under the Civil Code, you needed a judicial or

00:04:44.903 --> 00:04:48.305
extrajudicial constitution, and it took effect only on recording.

00:04:48.485 --> 00:04:53.306
Under the Family Code, from August third, nineteen eighty-eight, occupancy is enough.

00:04:53.836 --> 00:04:56.631
What about homes occupied before nineteen eighty-eight?

00:04:56.811 --> 00:05:02.699
Article one sixty-two applies the chapter to existing residences, but only prospectively.

00:05:02.879 --> 00:05:06.724
In Modequillo versus Breva, the liability arose from a nineteen seventy-six

00:05:06.724 --> 00:05:10.570
accident, so it was a debt incurred before the home became

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.716
a family home, and the property was not exempt.

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:17.659
Tolentino criticizes the occupancy rule as too simple, saying

00:05:17.659 --> 00:05:21.073
it may open the door to fraud against creditors.

00:05:22.153 --> 00:05:23.518
Who are the beneficiaries?

00:05:23.698 --> 00:05:26.258
Under Article one fifty-four, first, the spouses

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.818
or the unmarried head of the family.

00:05:28.998 --> 00:05:32.669
Second, their parents, ascendants, descendants, and brothers and sisters, legitimate

00:05:32.669 --> 00:05:36.340
or illegitimate, who live in the family home and depend

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.644
on the head of the family for legal support.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:43.267
So for a relative, there are three requisites: a

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:46.362
listed relationship, actual residence in the home, and dependence

00:05:46.362 --> 00:05:49.112
on the head of the family for support.

00:05:49.642 --> 00:05:51.263
Sir loves this situationer.

00:05:51.443 --> 00:05:53.406
The grandparents die in an accident.

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:56.943
Their five-year-old grandchild lives in the house, but his parents,

00:05:56.943 --> 00:05:59.965
who work in Manila, send money for his care.

00:06:00.145 --> 00:06:03.387
Is he a minor beneficiary who extends the family home?

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:04.250
No.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.578
He's only living there, and he doesn't

00:06:06.578 --> 00:06:08.419
depend on the grandparents for support.

00:06:08.599 --> 00:06:10.966
That's Patricio versus Dario, and it was

00:06:10.966 --> 00:06:12.994
asked in the twenty fourteen bar.

00:06:14.074 --> 00:06:16.912
Article one fifty-five lists the debts for which

00:06:16.912 --> 00:06:19.749
even a family home can be executed upon.

00:06:19.929 --> 00:06:21.678
Remember T, P, M, B.

00:06:21.858 --> 00:06:22.775
Taxes.

00:06:22.955 --> 00:06:25.131
Debts incurred prior to the constitution.

00:06:25.311 --> 00:06:27.907
Debts secured by a mortgage on the

00:06:27.907 --> 00:06:30.133
premises, before or after the constitution.

00:06:30.313 --> 00:06:32.737
And debts to builders, laborers and materialmen

00:06:32.737 --> 00:06:34.814
for the construction of the building.

00:06:35.344 --> 00:06:38.485
In Siari Valley Estates versus Lucasan, a judgment debt

00:06:38.485 --> 00:06:41.626
that was still on appeal when the family home

00:06:41.626 --> 00:06:44.069
was constituted was still a prior debt.

00:06:44.249 --> 00:06:46.297
It doesn't matter that it was disputed.

00:06:46.827 --> 00:06:47.830
Next, value.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:52.746
Under Article one fifty-seven, the family home cannot exceed three hundred thousand

00:06:52.746 --> 00:06:57.482
pesos in urban areas, or two hundred thousand pesos in rural areas,

00:06:57.482 --> 00:07:02.218
measured at the time of its constitution, not its market value today.

00:07:02.748 --> 00:07:06.702
And to sell, donate or mortgage it, Article one fifty-eight requires

00:07:06.702 --> 00:07:10.655
the written consent of the person who constituted it, his or

00:07:10.655 --> 00:07:14.609
her spouse, and a majority of the beneficiaries of legal age.

00:07:14.789 --> 00:07:16.773
Not all of them, and not the minors.

00:07:17.853 --> 00:07:19.922
What happens when the constitutors die?

00:07:20.102 --> 00:07:24.106
Under Article one fifty-nine, the family home continues for ten years,

00:07:24.106 --> 00:07:28.109
or for as long as there is a minor beneficiary, and

00:07:28.109 --> 00:07:32.113
the heirs cannot partition it unless the court finds compelling reasons.

00:07:32.293 --> 00:07:35.024
This applies regardless of who owns the property.

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:40.375
Article one sixty lets an ordinary creditor reach only the excess value.

00:07:40.555 --> 00:07:44.283
Say an urban family home sells for seven hundred fifty

00:07:44.283 --> 00:07:47.638
thousand pesos, and the judgment is three hundred thousand.

00:07:47.818 --> 00:07:51.558
The first three hundred thousand, the exempt amount, is applied first;

00:07:51.558 --> 00:07:55.297
then three hundred thousand goes to the creditor; and the remaining

00:07:55.297 --> 00:07:58.357
one hundred fifty thousand goes back to the debtor.

00:07:58.537 --> 00:08:01.993
And no bid below the family home value is even considered.

00:08:02.523 --> 00:08:04.635
Finally, you must claim the exemption.

00:08:04.815 --> 00:08:08.392
In De Mesa versus Acero, the Court said it's a personal right:

00:08:08.392 --> 00:08:11.969
it must be invoked and proved at the levy or within a

00:08:11.969 --> 00:08:15.546
reasonable time, and it is not the sheriff's duty to presume it.

00:08:16.075 --> 00:08:20.086
And in Salazar versus Felias, the claimant must prove that the

00:08:20.086 --> 00:08:24.096
home was duly constituted, by the proper persons, actually resided in,

00:08:24.096 --> 00:08:28.107
on the proper kind of property, and within the value limit.

00:08:29.187 --> 00:08:30.787
Part three, legitimacy.

00:08:30.967 --> 00:08:34.661
The core rule is Article one sixty-four: children conceived or

00:08:34.661 --> 00:08:37.986
born during the marriage of the parents are legitimate.

00:08:38.516 --> 00:08:39.711
Notice the word or.

00:08:39.891 --> 00:08:42.338
A child conceived before the wedding but

00:08:42.338 --> 00:08:44.435
born during the marriage is legitimate.

00:08:44.615 --> 00:08:47.837
So is a child conceived during the marriage but born

00:08:47.837 --> 00:08:50.737
after it ends, for example after the husband dies.

00:08:51.267 --> 00:08:54.830
Some children are legitimate even though the marriage is defective.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:09:00.759
Under Article fifty-four, children of a marriage void for psychological incapacity under

00:09:00.759 --> 00:09:06.508
Article thirty-six, conceived or born before the judgment becomes final, are legitimate.

00:09:06.688 --> 00:09:10.720
So are children of a subsequent marriage void under Article fifty-three.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:16.575
Children of voidable marriages, adopted children and legitimated children are legitimate too.

00:09:17.105 --> 00:09:20.287
Sir stresses that the Article fifty-four exception

00:09:20.287 --> 00:09:23.014
covers only Articles thirty-six and fifty-three.

00:09:23.194 --> 00:09:26.823
If the marriage is void for lack of a license, the children

00:09:26.823 --> 00:09:30.149
are illegitimate, and don't argue the best interest of the child.

00:09:30.329 --> 00:09:33.401
And in Quiz five, the statement that a legitimate

00:09:33.401 --> 00:09:36.473
child must be conceived or born during the marriage

00:09:36.473 --> 00:09:39.204
was false, because of these other legitimate children.

00:09:40.284 --> 00:09:45.212
The second paragraph of Article one sixty-four covers artificial insemination.

00:09:45.392 --> 00:09:49.883
A child conceived through insemination of the wife, with the sperm of

00:09:49.883 --> 00:09:54.374
the husband, a donor, or both, is legitimate, provided both spouses authorized

00:09:54.374 --> 00:09:58.491
or ratified it in a written instrument signed before the birth.

00:09:59.021 --> 00:10:01.602
Sir treats the written instrument as a requirement.

00:10:01.782 --> 00:10:05.985
In Quiz five, a statement that a child of insemination with the

00:10:05.985 --> 00:10:10.188
husband's sperm is legitimate, with no mention of written consent, was false.

00:10:10.368 --> 00:10:14.208
Watch for one changed word: if the item says public instrument

00:10:14.208 --> 00:10:18.048
instead of written instrument, the answer becomes none of the above.

00:10:18.228 --> 00:10:21.460
And if the embryo is carried by another woman,

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:24.692
that's surrogacy, which the Family Code does not recognize.

00:10:25.221 --> 00:10:28.383
Tolentino reads the writing as mere evidence of consent,

00:10:28.383 --> 00:10:31.194
and a twenty oh six bar answer agrees.

00:10:31.374 --> 00:10:34.724
But for Sir's class, treat the written instrument as required.

00:10:35.804 --> 00:10:40.604
Article one sixty-five is the mirror image: children conceived and born

00:10:40.604 --> 00:10:45.404
outside a valid marriage are illegitimate, unless the Code provides otherwise.

00:10:45.934 --> 00:10:47.043
Compare their rights.

00:10:47.223 --> 00:10:50.722
Legitimate children bear the surnames of the father and mother,

00:10:50.722 --> 00:10:54.221
are under joint parental authority, and get the full legitime.

00:10:54.401 --> 00:10:58.710
Illegitimate children use the mother's surname, though under Republic Act ninety-two

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:03.019
fifty-five they may use the father's if he expressly recognized them.

00:11:03.199 --> 00:11:06.371
They are under the mother's sole parental authority, and

00:11:06.371 --> 00:11:09.543
the legitime of each illegitimate child is one half

00:11:09.543 --> 00:11:12.010
of the legitime of a legitimate child.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.479
Two traps.

00:11:13.659 --> 00:11:16.080
Conceived or born outside a valid marriage

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.501
is false, because the codal says and.

00:11:18.681 --> 00:11:22.944
And one half of the legitime of the legitimate children is false:

00:11:22.944 --> 00:11:26.852
it's each illegitimate child getting half of one legitimate child's share.

00:11:27.382 --> 00:11:30.682
On surnames: in Osmeña de Valencia, legitimate children

00:11:30.682 --> 00:11:33.569
have no monopoly over their father's surname.

00:11:33.749 --> 00:11:36.320
In Barcelote, the word may is permissive, and

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:38.570
the mother must sign the birth certificate.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:42.569
And under Moore, a legitimate child can't take the stepfather's surname.

00:11:43.649 --> 00:11:45.953
Now, the action to impugn legitimacy.

00:11:46.133 --> 00:11:49.039
Article one sixty-six says legitimacy may be

00:11:49.039 --> 00:11:51.530
impugned only on its listed grounds.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:55.372
Look at this timeline: the three hundred days before birth, split into

00:11:55.372 --> 00:11:58.729
the first one hundred twenty and the last one hundred eighty.

00:11:58.909 --> 00:12:00.082
Why those numbers?

00:12:00.262 --> 00:12:03.345
Three hundred days is the longest gestation, and one

00:12:03.345 --> 00:12:06.428
hundred eighty is the shortest for a viable child.

00:12:06.608 --> 00:12:10.124
If the husband had no access in the first one hundred twenty

00:12:10.124 --> 00:12:13.640
days, conception could only have happened in the last one hundred eighty,

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:16.570
and a viable child couldn't have been born that soon.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:22.021
The first ground is physical impossibility of intercourse during that first one

00:12:22.021 --> 00:12:26.942
hundred twenty days, because of the husband's physical incapacity, meaning impotence and

00:12:26.942 --> 00:12:31.862
not sterility; because the spouses lived apart so that intercourse was impossible;

00:12:31.862 --> 00:12:35.553
or because of serious illness that absolutely prevented it.

00:12:36.083 --> 00:12:38.909
The second ground is biological or scientific

00:12:38.909 --> 00:12:41.331
proof, like blood tests or DNA.

00:12:41.511 --> 00:12:44.707
In Jao versus Court of Appeals, a blood test

00:12:44.707 --> 00:12:47.548
was conclusive of non-paternity, though not of paternity.

00:12:47.728 --> 00:12:51.782
The third ground is vitiated consent to artificial insemination.

00:12:52.312 --> 00:12:54.104
The cases show how strict this is.

00:12:54.284 --> 00:12:57.346
In Andal versus Macaraig, a husband with

00:12:57.346 --> 00:13:00.407
advanced tuberculosis was still capable of intercourse.

00:13:00.587 --> 00:13:05.336
In Macadangdang, the spouses lived in the same province, so access

00:13:05.336 --> 00:13:09.653
was possible, and estrangement alone is moral, not physical, impossibility.

00:13:09.833 --> 00:13:13.652
And in Tan versus Trocio, physical resemblance proved nothing.

00:13:14.732 --> 00:13:19.269
Article one sixty-seven: the child is still legitimate even if the

00:13:19.269 --> 00:13:23.393
mother declares against its legitimacy, or is convicted of adultery.

00:13:23.573 --> 00:13:25.771
Her word doesn't decide the child's status.

00:13:26.301 --> 00:13:29.678
Article one sixty-eight handles a mother who remarries within

00:13:29.678 --> 00:13:32.680
three hundred days after her first marriage ends.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:36.110
If the child is born within one hundred eighty days

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:39.359
after the second wedding, and also within three hundred days

00:13:39.359 --> 00:13:42.609
of the termination, the child is presumed the first husband's.

00:13:42.789 --> 00:13:45.722
If born after one hundred eighty days from the

00:13:45.722 --> 00:13:48.656
second wedding, the child is presumed the second husband's.

00:13:49.185 --> 00:13:50.892
Here's Sir's Quiz five problem.

00:13:51.072 --> 00:13:53.760
A dies on January first, twenty twenty-four.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.201
His widow B marries C on August first.

00:13:56.381 --> 00:13:58.386
D is born on November fifteenth.

00:13:58.566 --> 00:14:01.390
That's three hundred nineteen days after A's death, beyond

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:03.900
three hundred, so A cannot be the father.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:06.256
The one-eighty rule doesn't even matter.

00:14:06.436 --> 00:14:08.538
D is the legitimate child of B

00:14:08.538 --> 00:14:10.340
and C, born during their marriage.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.804
And under Article one sixty-nine, if a child is

00:14:13.804 --> 00:14:16.737
born more than three hundred days after the marriage

00:14:16.737 --> 00:14:19.019
ended, there is no presumption either way.

00:14:19.199 --> 00:14:22.805
Whoever alleges legitimacy or illegitimacy must prove it.

00:14:23.885 --> 00:14:25.506
How long does the husband have?

00:14:25.686 --> 00:14:29.145
Under Article one seventy: one year, if he or any

00:14:29.145 --> 00:14:32.605
heir lives in the city or municipality where the birth

00:14:32.605 --> 00:14:36.064
took place or was recorded; two years if elsewhere in

00:14:36.064 --> 00:14:38.486
the Philippines; and three years if abroad.

00:14:38.666 --> 00:14:42.367
The period runs from knowledge of the birth or its recording,

00:14:42.367 --> 00:14:46.069
or if the birth was concealed, from discovery, whichever is earlier.

00:14:46.599 --> 00:14:50.873
Under Article one seventy-one, the heirs may impugn only in three

00:14:50.873 --> 00:14:55.146
cases: the husband died before his period expired; he died after

00:14:55.146 --> 00:14:59.420
filing without desisting; or the child was born after his death.

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:01.145
Who else can impugn?

00:15:01.325 --> 00:15:04.101
Under Liyao, only the husband or his heirs;

00:15:04.101 --> 00:15:06.530
the child cannot choose his own filiation.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:10.870
But Yap versus Yap, in twenty twenty-two, allowed a child

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:15.030
to establish filiation with his biological father despite the presumption.

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:17.962
Sir agrees with Yap: truth over reputation.

00:15:18.142 --> 00:15:21.150
In recitation, give the rule, then Yap and Sir's view.

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:22.661
Three traps.

00:15:22.841 --> 00:15:25.870
In Quiz five, Sir changed city or municipality to

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:28.900
country, which makes the answer none of the above.

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:33.248
A child whose legitimacy is successfully impugned is not an illegitimate

00:15:33.248 --> 00:15:37.037
child of the spouses; he's simply not the husband's child.

00:15:37.217 --> 00:15:39.671
And legitimacy can't be attacked collaterally.

00:15:39.851 --> 00:15:42.930
But under Lim versus Intermediate Appellate Court, a claim

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:46.010
that someone is not the child at all is

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:48.405
not impugning, so these periods don't apply.

00:15:49.485 --> 00:15:51.320
Part four, proof of filiation.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:56.030
Article one seventy-two has primary evidence: the record of birth in the

00:15:56.030 --> 00:16:00.559
civil register or a final judgment, and an admission of filiation in

00:16:00.559 --> 00:16:05.089
a public document or a private handwritten instrument signed by the parent.

00:16:05.619 --> 00:16:10.183
Secondary evidence is allowed only in the absence of primary evidence: open

00:16:10.183 --> 00:16:14.747
and continuous possession of the status of a child, or any other

00:16:14.747 --> 00:16:18.931
means allowed by the Rules of Court, like testimony or DNA.

00:16:19.111 --> 00:16:23.079
Mendoza versus Court of Appeals says the father must treat

00:16:23.079 --> 00:16:27.047
the child as his own, directly, spontaneously, and not intermittently.

00:16:27.577 --> 00:16:29.092
What's not enough by itself?

00:16:29.272 --> 00:16:31.491
A birth certificate the father didn't sign,

00:16:31.491 --> 00:16:33.709
as in Reyes versus Court of Appeals.

00:16:33.889 --> 00:16:36.492
As Sir put it, you could write anyone's name on it.

00:16:36.672 --> 00:16:41.792
Baptismal certificates, a marriage contract, photos and resemblance aren't enough either.

00:16:42.322 --> 00:16:46.095
Under Article one seventy-five, illegitimate children prove filiation the

00:16:46.095 --> 00:16:49.869
same way, but if they rely on secondary evidence,

00:16:49.869 --> 00:16:53.223
they must sue during the alleged parent's lifetime.

00:16:53.403 --> 00:16:57.585
Sir thinks this is regressive, given DNA, and cites Aquino and Yap.

00:16:57.765 --> 00:17:00.656
But his quiz keys follow the codal, so answer with

00:17:00.656 --> 00:17:03.546
the lifetime rule, and add his view if there's room.

00:17:04.626 --> 00:17:06.077
Last, legitimation.

00:17:06.257 --> 00:17:10.263
Under Article one seventy-seven, as amended by Republic Act ninety-eight

00:17:10.263 --> 00:17:14.270
fifty-eight, children conceived and born outside of wedlock may be

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:18.276
legitimated if, at the time of conception, their parents were

00:17:18.276 --> 00:17:22.283
not disqualified by any impediment to marry each other, or

00:17:22.283 --> 00:17:26.289
were disqualified only because one or both were below eighteen.

00:17:26.819 --> 00:17:28.099
So there are three steps.

00:17:28.279 --> 00:17:29.986
No impediment at conception.

00:17:30.166 --> 00:17:34.475
A subsequent valid marriage of the parents, under Article one seventy-eight.

00:17:34.655 --> 00:17:36.998
And then the effect retroacts to the

00:17:36.998 --> 00:17:39.007
child's birth, under Article one eighty.

00:17:39.537 --> 00:17:42.524
Sir's points: what matters is the time of conception.

00:17:42.704 --> 00:17:46.629
An impediment that arises only by the time of birth doesn't matter.

00:17:46.809 --> 00:17:49.774
Age is a matter of capacity, not an impediment.

00:17:49.954 --> 00:17:52.589
The codal says may be legitimated, not will

00:17:52.589 --> 00:17:55.224
be, because a valid marriage is still needed.

00:17:55.404 --> 00:17:58.177
And in an essay, first establish that

00:17:58.177 --> 00:18:00.950
the child is illegitimate, then discuss legitimation.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:02.611
A few more rules.

00:18:02.791 --> 00:18:06.000
Annulment of a voidable marriage doesn't undo legitimation,

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:08.807
but a void marriage legitimates no one.

00:18:08.987 --> 00:18:13.445
Legitimation of a child who died before the marriage benefits his descendants.

00:18:13.625 --> 00:18:16.572
And legitimation may be impugned only by those

00:18:16.572 --> 00:18:19.151
prejudiced in their rights, within five years.

00:18:20.231 --> 00:18:21.170
Let's recap.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:25.936
One: Article one fifty lists four relations, and in-laws are strangers.

00:18:26.116 --> 00:18:30.273
Two: earnest efforts applies only if all parties are family, the

00:18:30.273 --> 00:18:34.052
subject is compromisable, and the defense is raised on time.

00:18:34.582 --> 00:18:38.668
Three: the family home is constituted by occupancy, and

00:18:38.668 --> 00:18:42.753
homes occupied before nineteen eighty-eight are covered only prospectively.

00:18:42.933 --> 00:18:45.439
Four: a beneficiary must be related, live there,

00:18:45.439 --> 00:18:47.946
and depend on the head of the family.

00:18:48.126 --> 00:18:51.528
Five: remember T, P, M, B, the value limits

00:18:51.528 --> 00:18:54.931
at constitution, and claim the exemption at the levy.

00:18:55.461 --> 00:18:59.696
Six: conceived or born during the marriage means legitimate,

00:18:59.696 --> 00:19:03.930
and Article fifty-four covers only Articles thirty-six and fifty-three.

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:07.492
Seven: for Sir, artificial insemination needs written

00:19:07.492 --> 00:19:10.873
consent before birth, and surrogacy isn't recognized.

00:19:11.053 --> 00:19:14.999
Eight: the first one hundred twenty of three hundred days, and one,

00:19:14.999 --> 00:19:18.946
two or three years to impugn, counted from whichever date is earlier.

00:19:19.477 --> 00:19:23.403
Nine: secondary proof of illegitimate filiation needs the parent alive

00:19:23.403 --> 00:19:27.328
under the codal, though Sir would allow DNA after death.

00:19:27.508 --> 00:19:31.032
And ten: for legitimation, test the impediment at conception,

00:19:31.032 --> 00:19:34.164
and remember that age is not an impediment.

00:19:34.344 --> 00:19:36.968
Good luck in recitation and on Monday's quiz.
